hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23873","Rawh narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us from Hassan ibn Atiyyah from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Dhu Mikhmar, a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Romans will make a secure truce with you, then you will raid them with a raid and be helped and safe and take booty, then you will leave until you camp at a meadow with hills, so a man of the Christians will raise a cross and say: The cross has overcome, so a man of the Muslims will grow angry and stand to him and smash him, then at that the Romans will betray and gather for the great battle, and Rawh once said: And you will be safe and take booty and stay, then you will leave."
"23874","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Sha'bi narrated to me who said: I asked Ibn Umar, I said: Does a camel and a cow suffice for seven, he said: He said: O Sha'bi, does it have seven souls, he said: I said: The companions of Muhammad claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sanctioned a camel and a cow for seven, he said: So Ibn Umar said to a man: Is it so, O so-and-so, he said: Yes, he said: I did not know of this."
